Definitions

Developer means a person who writes or modifies code that imports Formrail Pro. Build systems, continuous
integration and the end users of your application are not developers for these terms and do not need a
license.

Licensed developer means a developer for whom you hold a license under these terms.

Production use means running an application that includes Formrail Pro, or code built from it, for real users
or for the day-to-day business of an organization. Development and evaluation are not production use.

Update period means the 12 months described in the section Term and updates.

Covered version means any version of Formrail Pro that is published during your update period.

Registry means the private package registry on GitHub Packages from which Formrail Pro is distributed.

Grant

For each license you buy, the licensor grants you a non-exclusive, non-transferable, worldwide license for one
licensed developer to use, copy and modify the covered versions of Formrail Pro, and to include them in the
applications you build, on the terms of this document.

The license is per developer. It is held by one named person at a time, and one license cannot be shared by
several people at the same time. The number of developers who may work on code that imports Formrail Pro in
production applications is the number of licenses you hold.

You may use the covered versions in as many applications as you build, and you may ship those applications,
with Formrail Pro built into them, to their end users. End users need no license of their own.

Formrail Pro does not check for a license at runtime and needs no key. These terms are a legal agreement, not
a technical lock.

Term and updates

You pay once. The payment gives you access to the registry and to every version published during 12 months of
updates. The 12 months start on the day access to the registry is granted to you, not on the day of the
purchase.

The license does not renew automatically, and you are not charged again unless you choose to buy again.

After the term

When the 12 months end, your access to the registry ends, but your right to use what you already have does
not. You may keep using every covered version, in development and in production, with no limit of time, and
you may keep building and shipping applications with it. Ending the registry access is not a revocation of the
license.

Versions published after the end of your update period are not covered. To use them, you need to buy a new
license. The number of licensed developers stays the number you bought, and the use of the covered versions
stays subject to these terms, including the section Restrictions.

Evaluation and development use

You may use Formrail Pro freely, with no license and no payment, to evaluate it and to develop and test
applications on development machines and in test environments that real users do not use. This includes
reading the source in the public repository and exploring the Pro demo on formrail.dev. There is no fixed time
limit, but evaluation and development are not production use.

Production use

A license is required for production use. For an application in production use, every developer who writes or
modifies code that imports Formrail Pro in that application must be a licensed developer.

Replacing a developer

If a licensed developer leaves your team, you can replace them with another person. Write to
formrail.dev@gmail.com, and the license and the registry access are moved to the new developer. The number of
licensed developers does not change, the license cannot be held by two people at the same time, and the
replacement receives only what is left of the update period: it does not start a new 12 months.

Restrictions

You may not sell, sublicense, rent, lend or give Formrail Pro, or a copy of it, to others, as a package, a
library or a set of components, whether modified or not. Shipping it built into your own application, as
described in the section Grant, is allowed.

You may not share registry access or access tokens with people who are not licensed developers, and you may
not remove the copyright and license notices from Formrail Pro.

Reading the source in the public repository does not grant any right beyond the ones in these terms.

Early access status

Formrail Pro is in early access. Its versions are 0.x, and the API can change between versions, including in
ways that require changes in your code.

No release date, roadmap item or feature is promised. The licensor is not obliged to deliver any feature that
is not in a version already published. During your update period you receive the versions that are published,
whatever they contain.

Support

Support is given by email at formrail.dev@gmail.com, on a best-effort basis. We aim to reply within 2 business
days. This is a target and not a guarantee, and it is not a time to fix a problem. Support covers the use of
Formrail Pro during your update period.

Refunds

You can ask for a refund within 14 days of the purchase, without giving a reason, whoever you are. The details
are on the refund page: https://formrail.dev/refund/

